codemap 9
tour feature-promote
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note promote <symbol> [depth] [name] [--all]: create (or extend) a flow shaped like a symbol's call tree, depth levels deep (default 2), pruned unless --all: tests, accessors (3 lines or fewer with 3 or more callers) and trivial bodies are left out, and callees that are shared (3 or more callers), in another package, or already mapped by another tour are kept as leaves; the report names each rule's symbols and prints a step-link line for each mapped leaf, named after the symbol unless name is given. The agent reaches for it to scaffold a flow from a call tree instead of adding every step by hand. It is scaffolding: the tree comes from xrefs, so it carries every helper and, with only the tree-sitter resolver, some false calls; the author trims it with tour-rm and tour-move and writes the notes. Re-running it on the same tour reuses the steps a symbol already has instead of duplicating them.

